  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Organisations pay for people who understand customers, employees and communities and can explain what the evidence says. They judge you by clarity and rigour.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is turning a research finding into one practical recommendation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and social science and sociology graduates in business roles: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools summarise literature, code responses and draft reports. Routine analysis shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Research judgment, ethics and context hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to summarise and check; later, own interpretation and recommendations.
  </p>

